#+TITLE: Remaining alfe test portability failures on Windows
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS:
#+BRANCH:

* Observations (2026-10-07)
Running autolisp-front-end/tests on SBCL on Windows exposed three failures
outside the backend discovery and parity fixes:
- actions-load-missing-file expects a drive-less POSIX path in stderr.
- kill-engine-process-is-bounded-not-blocking cannot launch sh when MSYS
  executables are absent from PATH in a native PowerShell session.
- autocad-build-launch-argv-batch-discovers-template-and-still-requires-accoreconsole
  compares a drive-qualified drawing path against a drive-less workdir.

* Reproduction
Load the clautolisp and autolisp-front-end ASDF definitions, then run
asdf:test-system on autolisp-front-end under native SBCL on Windows.

* Work
Make pathname expectations portable without weakening their checks. Review
the process fixture's shell dependency and document or replace it.
